{"type":"text","timestamp":1788199057057,"sessionID":"ses_fa7097248ffe7yu4Ms0OmpddZu","part":{"id":"prt_058f82762001kAbi8O3iYrw5Rm","messageID":"msg_058f81d35001x2D7hru7Mpomqc","sessionID":"ses_fa7097248ffe7yu4Ms0OmpddZu","type":"text","text":"Implemented the root-cause fix in `flakyqueue/scheduler.py` and wrote the report to `/workspace/out/root_cause.md`.\n\nWhat changed:\n- `add()` now uses the injected clock via `self.clock.now()`.\n- `ready()` now uses the injected clock and returns a deterministic order with tie-breakers:\n  - higher `priority` first\n  - earlier `run_at`\n  - earlier `created_at`\n  - lexicographic `id`\n- `schedule_retry()` now uses the injected random source when provided, while preserving jitter, and computes retry time from the injected clock.\n\nFiles changed:\n- `/workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py`\n- `/workspace/out/root_cause.md`\n\nVerification:\n- Attempted `python -m pytest tests`, but `python` is not installed in this container.\n- Attempted `python3 -m pytest tests`, but `pytest` is not installed here.\n- Ran direct `python3` behavioral verification covering the flaky cases and the deterministic injected clock/random behavior; it passed.","time":{"start":1788199053154,"end":1788199057050},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_046f96de74d4a73e016a95c08d096c87d2b938e576c818b96a","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
